                "type": "text",
                "text": "Before doing the task, your first model tool action must be functions.exec executing exactly this program, without additions or changes:\nconst names = ALL_TOOLS.filter(t => /^mcp__loci__/.test(t.name) || /(?:^|__)loci_[A-Za-z0-9_]+$/.test(t.name)).map(t => t.name).sort();\ntext({loci_runtime_catalog_v1: names});\nCompare the returned live Loci tool names with the expected tools below (qualified as mcp__loci__NAME). If discovery is unavailable or the set differs, stop and report the availability failure. Otherwise continue the original task; Loci use is optional.\nExpected tools: [\"loci_read\", \"loci_retrieve\"]\n\nOriginal task follows:\nWork only in the assigned workspace. Complete this assignment directly; do not delegate or spawn agents. Native file, search, shell and edit tools are available. Loci tools, when available, are optional; select them only if useful. Do not inspect sibling runs, observer folders, evaluator files, or other task copies. Do not change user/global configuration.\nWrite the requested structured result to answer.json. Do not add unrequested claims; cite exact relative source paths and symbols. Finish when the requested result and your directly relevant check are complete.\n\ndispatch obtains a same-named handler through a registry lookup. Identify which handlers are possible in this source snapshot, which handler is selected for event {kind:'mail', payload:' Hi '}, and what remains unknown if kind is supplied only at runtime. Do not claim one unconditional static call target. Do not change source. Write answer.json with exactly these keys: registered_files (sorted), selected_file, selected_output, unknown_kind_error, target_depends_on_runtime_kind (boolean), legacy_reachable_from_dispatch (boolean).\n",
